Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Mirrored Traffic Not Appearing
Symptoms: Staging version (v2) not receiving any traffic

Solution:

# Check virtual service configuration
kubectl describe virtualservice bookinfo-mirror -n traffic-mirror-lab

# Verify destination rules
kubectl get destinationrule -n traffic-mirror-lab

# Check Istio proxy configuration
kubectl exec -n traffic-mirror-lab deployment/productpage-v1 -c istio-proxy -- \
  pilot-agent request GET config_dump | grep -A 20 mirror
Issue 2: High Resource Usage
Symptoms: Pods consuming too much CPU/Memory

Solution:

# Check resource usage
kubectl top pods -n traffic-mirror-lab

# Reduce mirror percentage
kubectl patch virtualservice bookinfo-mirror -n traffic-mirror-lab --type='merge' \
  -p='{"spec":{"http":[{"match":[{"uri":{"exact":"/productpage"}}],"route":[{"destination":{"host":"productpage","subset":"v1"},"weight":100}],"mirror":{"host":"productpage","subset":"v2"},"mirrorPercentage":{"value":10.0}}]}}'
Issue 3: Gateway Not Accessible
Symptoms: Cannot access application through ingress gateway

Solution:

# Check gateway status
kubectl get gateway -n traffic-mirror-lab

# Verify ingress gateway service
kubectl get svc istio-ingressgateway -n istio-system

# Check gateway configuration
kubectl describe gateway bookinfo-gateway -n traffic-mirror-lab
Advanced Configuration Options
Option 1: Header-Based Mirroring
Create selective mirroring based on request headers:

apiVersion: networking.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: VirtualService
metadata:
  name: bookinfo-header-mirror
  namespace: traffic-mirror-lab
spec:
  hosts:
  - "*"
  gateways:
  - bookinfo-gateway
  http:
  - match:
    - headers:
        x-mirror-test:
          exact: "true"
    route:
    - destination:
        host: productpage
        subset: v1
      weight: 100
    mirror:
      host: productpage
      subset: v2
    mirrorPercentage:
      value: 100.0
  - route:
    - destination:
        host: productpage
        subset: v1
      weight: 100
Option 2: Time-Based Mirroring
Implement time-based traffic mirroring:

# Create a cron job for time-based mirroring
kubectl create job mirror-scheduler --image=curlimages/curl -- \
  /bin/sh -c "
  # Enable mirroring during business hours (9 AM - 5 PM)
  current_hour=\$(date +%H)
  if [ \$current_hour -ge 9 ] && [ \$current_hour -le 17 ]; then
    kubectl patch virtualservice bookinfo-mirror -n traffic-mirror-lab --type='merge' \
      -p='{\"spec\":{\"http\":[{\"mirrorPercentage\":{\"value\":100.0}}]}}'
  else
    kubectl patch virtualservice bookinfo-mirror -n traffic-mirror-lab --type='merge' \
      -p='{\"spec\":{\"http\":[{\"mirrorPercentage\":{\"value\":0.0}}]}}'
  fi
  "
